{"name":"Native Hue of Resolution","hex":"#d33300","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"native","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Belonging to one by birth or ancestry.","Characteristic of or relating to people inhabiting a region from prehistoric times."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who is native to a place; a person who was born in a place.","A person of aboriginal descent, as distinguished from a person who was or whose ancestors were foreigners or settlers/colonizers. Alternative letter-case form of Native (aboriginal inhabitant of the Americas or Australia)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/native"},{"term":"hue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color, or shade of color; tint; dye.","The characteristic related to the light frequency that appears in the color, for instance red, yellow, green, cyan, blue or magenta."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shout or cry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hue"},{"term":"resolution","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A firm decision or an official decision.","A strong will; the state of being resolute."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/resolution"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hue","blocks":[{"text":"In color theory, hue is one of the properties of a color, defined in the CIECAM02 model as \"the degree to which a stimulus can be described as similar to or different from stimuli that are described as red, orange, yellow, green, blue, violet\", within certain theories of color vision."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Colors-i54-ring.png/330px-Colors-i54-ring.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hue","wikidata":"Q372948"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Munsell_hue_wheel_equal_value_and_chroma.png/500px-Munsell_hue_wheel_equal_value_and_chroma.png?utm_